## Slide 3

Considerations

Data Processing

Why
Allows users to implement business logic in the interface. Common examples include the ability to merge data from a payload into a single field for mapping to TrakSYS entities.
Parameters Passed
When interfaces transactions trigger post process actions like DMS and Workflow. Some parameters are passed onto the next step as arguments, such as: Interface Definition ID, Interface Definition Key, and Interface Transaction ID.
Orchestration Options
	DMS
	Ideal for processing a single interface transaction.
	Workflow 
	Ideal for organizing events around an interface transaction.
	Plugin 
	Ideal for interacting with the interface transaction data before it’s passed downstream and/or for processing synchronously.